00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:04.160
Jack: So, what are the advantages and
disadvantages of functional, object

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:06.080
oriented and other coding types.

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:09.280
Leah: Let’s start by
looking at Functional coding

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:12.130
The Advantages of Functional coding are:

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:17.560
- It’s easy to debug [no side effects
or hidden inputs or outputs]

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:21.549
- Functions are easier to understand
because they do not affect any

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:23.350
variables outside of themself.

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:26.680
The Disadvantages of
Functional coding are:

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:29.989
- The type of function used can
reduce the readability of the code.

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:34.460
- Using recursive functions instead
of loops can take a while to learn.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:39.080
Jack: Now let’s look at Object
Oriented Programming [OOP]

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:42.830
The Advantages of Object
Oriented Programming are:

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:46.460
- It is very mature and
professionally appreciated.

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:49.740
- It is also good for making
sophisticated software.

00:00:50.799 --> 00:00:53.959
The Disadvantages of Object
Oriented Programming are:

00:00:54.770 --> 00:00:56.730
- It involves a steep learning curve.

00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:00.430
- Large programs end up with
slower operating speeds.

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:03.699
Leah: Let’s look at
some other coding types.

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:07.750
We have already looked at how
imperative and declarative coding

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:11.779
differs so let’s now look at the
advantages and disadvantages of

00:01:11.779 --> 00:01:13.800
imperative and declarative coding.

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:20.780
Jack: Imperative coding is a relatively
simple concept, and it simplifies code

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:26.280
by reusing code sections, however,
there is a higher risk of making errors

00:01:26.289 --> 00:01:29.859
when compared with declarative and
it can quickly become complicated.

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:34.380
This makes maintenance, optimisation,
and extension difficult.

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:40.160
Leah: Declarative coding is clearer than
imperative coding and we have mentioned

00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:45.080
is easier to extend, but it can be more
difficult to understand for someone who

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:47.570
is not a domain specific specialist.

00:01:48.619 --> 00:01:53.160
Jack: With Procedural coding it is easy
to track the flow of a program and it is

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:55.830
also easy to implement, debug and adapt.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:02:00.720
However, it can be hard to write
and far abstracted from reality.

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:06.390
Leah: Logic programming is a rather high
level of coding which has good memory

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:08.580
management being fast and efficient.

00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:13.150
But it can be difficult to apply in
more general contexts of computation.

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:17.899
Jack: Parallel processing is more
efficient than with sequential

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:23.270
programming as it reaches the outcome
quicker, but it can be more complex

00:02:23.270 --> 00:02:27.619
to write, difficult to scale and has
potentially higher resource requirements.

